From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: refactor check wed module busy time

change timeout from 1.5s to 100ms. Without this patch, L1 SER may spend
5s in heavy bi-di traffic and wed module can not go back to the idle
state. It will cause some stations disconnect.

Vendor source: MediaTek mtk-openwrt-feeds 25.12 patch 999-wed-20.
Signed-off-by: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>

Applicability (local, 2026-09-27): mtk_wed_poll_busy() carries no
NETSYSv1/v2/v3 gate - it is the shared busy-wait helper used by every
WED generation's start/stop/reset paths, confirmed unmodified at this
tree's built drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c:276-285 before this
patch. Previously deferred pending an A/B (see docs/README.md's Current
open work), because the fork's traffic record was single-client and
this board's WED-v1 path saw comparatively little sustained load.

Now applicable: live traffic evidence (2026-09-27 evaluation) shows the
RAX70 wireless-repeater backhaul keeps wl1-ap0's WED-v1 path in
continuous bidirectional traffic - one station measured at ~27% of its
own connected time in TX and a nonzero RX duty cycle, all day, not a
short burst. That is exactly the "heavy bi-di traffic" condition the
vendor's own commit message names as the trigger for the 1.5s stall.
Shortening the poll interval (15ms -> 1ms) and the overall timeout
(1.5s -> 100ms) bounds how long any mtk_wed_poll_busy() caller can block
during that condition, including this fork's own WED-v1 SER recovery
patches (999-wed-13, 999-wed-14).

Hardware caveat: this router has produced zero WED/mt7915 SER events in
the observed uptime, so the specific station-disconnect symptom has not
been reproduced live on this board - the case for carrying this patch
now rests on the vendor's stated failure mode matching this
deployment's confirmed traffic shape, not on a local reproduction. Flash
and monitor `logread -e mt7915-ser-watchdog` after the next real SER
event to confirm no regression.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -276,7 +276,7 @@
 static int
 mtk_wed_poll_busy(struct mtk_wed_device *dev, u32 reg, u32 mask)
 {
-	int sleep = 15000;
+	int sleep = 1000;
 	int timeout = 100 * sleep;
 	u32 val;
 
